{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mathematical game balance mathematical game balance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md","fileName":"Mathematical Game Balance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mathematical Game Balance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Balance and Progression]] [[Game Analytics and Probability]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Analytics and Probability","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mathematical game balance mathematical game balance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md","fileName":"Mathematical Game Balance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mathematical Game Balance","heading":"Mathematical Game Balance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Mathematical game balance uses equations, probability, and forward-looking models to set relationships among costs, benefits, power, and progression. It helps expose strongly unbalanced parts before extensive play data exists.\n\nModels are tools rather than complete answers: they cannot decide the desired experience or eliminate all interaction effects in a complex game. Their predictions still need designer judgment and [[Playtesting]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Analytics and Probability","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Game Balance.md: